#
# macOS: QtBluetooth's Objective-C classes on the 32-bit runtime (the i386
# port).
#
# The 32-bit (fragile) Objective-C runtime fixes each instance variable's
# offset when the class is compiled, from its @interface, and so accepts
# instance variables only there - not in the @implementation, not in a class
# extension - and synthesizes no property by itself. Qt 5.15 was written for
# the 64-bit runtime only.
#
# The twelve IOBluetooth and CoreBluetooth wrapper classes declare their
# variables in the @interface, in their private headers, which now include
# what those variables need. The LE device inquiry's members are CoreBluetooth
# types (10.7); like its implementation (patch 39) they are exempt from the
# availability errors, since the class is created only where CoreBluetooth
# exists.
#
# Nothing changes in behaviour, on any architecture.
#
# Apply: git apply, from the Qt source root
